{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>He has not beheld iniquity.</b> In my opinion, from this word Balak learned to send the women of Moab into the camp of Israel. The meaning is that HaShem is not like a mortal that He should change His mind, for He saw no iniquity in Israel. Now if there be iniquity in them, the word of HaShem will not stand, for all His words are conditional, except in the case of an oath. And so the prophet says, <i>For a moment I speak</i> [Isaiah 54:7]. And this is the meaning of Balaam's word." "<b>Nor has He seen trouble.</b> The meaning is doubled, and it is the cognate of און. The sense: what does a man bring to trouble in the wake of iniquity. And so at every time that He has not beheld iniquity in Jacob, HaShem is with him." "<b>And the king's tru'ah is in him.</b> In the camp of Israel. And this is <i>and you shall sound a tru'ah</i> [Numbers 10:5]."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:12.873917094Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}